    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Evaluate $\\frac{9!}{6!\\times3!}$ without a calculator.",
    "solution_text": "Unroll $9!$ until $6!$ appears, and use $3!=6$.\n\n$\\begin{align*} &\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\frac{9!}{6!\\times3!}\\\\ &=\\frac{9\\times8\\times7\\times6!}{6!\\times6}\\\\ &=\\frac{9\\times8\\times7}{6}\\\\ &=84 \\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Simplify $\\frac{(n+4)!}{(n+2)!}$ fully, where $n$ is a non-negative integer.",
    "solution_text": "$\\begin{align*} &\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\frac{(n+4)!}{(n+2)!}\\\\ &=\\frac{(n+4)(n+3)(n+2)!}{(n+2)!}\\\\ &=(n+4)(n+3)\\\\ &=n^2+7n+12 \\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Simplify $\\frac{(n-3)!}{n!}$, where $n$ is an integer with $n\\ge3$.",
    "solution_text": "$\\begin{align*} &\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\frac{(n-3)!}{n!}\\\\ &=\\frac{(n-3)!}{n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3)!}\\\\ &=\\frac{1}{n(n-1)(n-2)} \\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Simplify $\\frac{(n-2)!(n+3)!}{(n+2)!(n-3)!}$ fully, where $n$ is an integer with $n\\ge3$.",
    "solution_text": "$\\begin{align*} &\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\frac{(n-2)!(n+3)!}{(n+2)!(n-3)!}\\\\ &=\\frac{(n-2)(n-3)!\\times(n+3)(n+2)!}{(n+2)!(n-3)!}\\\\ &=(n-2)(n+3)\\\\ &=n^2+n-6 \\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Express $(n+3)!+(n+2)!+(n+1)!$ in the form $P(n)\\times(n+1)!$, where $P(n)$ is a polynomial and $n$ is a non-negative integer.",
    "solution_text": "Take out the smallest factorial, $(n+1)!$.\n\n$\\begin{align*} &\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}(n+3)!+(n+2)!+(n+1)!\\\\ &=(n+3)(n+2)(n+1)!+(n+2)(n+1)!+(n+1)!\\\\ &=\\big((n+3)(n+2)+(n+2)+1\\big)(n+1)!\\\\ &=(n^2+6n+9)(n+1)!\\\\ &=(n+3)^2(n+1)! \\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Write $\\frac{1}{(n+1)!}-\\frac{1}{(n+3)!}$ as a single fraction in simplest form, where $n$ is a non-negative integer.",
    "solution_text": "Use $(n+3)!=(n+3)(n+2)(n+1)!$ to obtain a common denominator.\n\n$\\begin{align*} &\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\frac{1}{(n+1)!}-\\frac{1}{(n+3)!}\\\\ &=\\frac{(n+3)(n+2)}{(n+3)!}-\\frac{1}{(n+3)!}\\\\ &=\\frac{(n+3)(n+2)-1}{(n+3)!}\\\\ &=\\frac{n^2+5n+5}{(n+3)!} \\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  }
]
